emy  you're nearly convinced that michael  might just send a second employee to the  hospital  lucky for toby the prank is obvious and  michael doesn't succeed  but for a moment the audience is  perfectly suspended between horror and  hilarity  who could have imagined that phyllis  with her love of gaudy makeovers  charming handicrafts and overwhelming  perfume would have ended up so truly  bizarre  her marriage went from being a lovely  facet of the office park to the most  sexual relationship on the show  she took revenge on angela for crimes  committed in the name of party planning  and hey remember that time she revealed  that she gave up a child for adoption  and wondered if aaron might be that very  baby  phyllis's deaths were strange funny and  often pretty endearing  but in one deleted scene things take a  turn for the wildly morbid  phyllis straight up confesses to  manslaughter that she and bob  only narrowly got away with a crime she  isn't even able to convince herself into  dismissing  it's humor so dark that it makes sense  that it was cut but as a deleted scene  cast into the quasi-canon of the show  it's truly horrifically hilarious  before andy was in and out of love with  aaron before he was the boss  he was a fumbling salesman with nothing  but a cornell degree to his name  among the earliest hits he would take  was the moment he realized the young  woman he'd been seeing was  in fact an underage high schooler the  office pulled a bit more comedy from the  otherwise criminal situation in this  deleted scene  andy cartoonishly confronts his  girlfriend jim attempts to keep andy  from incriminating himself  and it becomes more and more clear just  how thoroughly she and her friends were  using him for access to the adult world  cutting this scene made the plotline  more focused on andy's failure to  establish himself in scranton  and made it less cringe-worthy sometimes  comedy comes from the stuff you don't  see  it makes sense that we don't get to